><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1575" y="444"/><mxPoint x="1575" y="88"/><mxPoint x="800" y="88"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c45" value="GET /health" style="html=1;rounded=0;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeColor=#1F2933;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=11;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#1F2933;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c27" target="c9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1410" y="655"/><mxPoint x="670" y="655"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c46" value="&lt;b&gt;Main workflow — student submits a food request&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1.  Student fills an HTML form; the browser POSTs it with the session cookie and a CSRF token.&lt;br&gt;2.  Middleware rejects the call if the CSRF token is wrong, then loads the user from the session.&lt;br&gt;3.  Permission check: the user must be in the Student group; then the view function runs.&lt;br&gt;4.  The view validates the form (slot capacity, not in the past) and saves through the ORM.&lt;br&gt;5.  transaction.atomic(): the request row and the audit_log row commit together or not at all.&lt;br&gt;6.  After commit, send_mail() runs in the same process (short timeout). No queue to operate.&lt;br&gt;7.  SMTP service delivers the confirmation; on failure Django logs the error.&lt;br&gt;8.  Server redirects (302) and the browser loads the rendered “Request submitted” page." style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#1F2933;rounded=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#FFFDF2;strokeColor=#C9B458;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;spacingRight=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="680" width="1000" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c47" value="" style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontColor=#1F2933;rounded=1;arcSize=4;fillColor=#FFFDF2;strokeColor=#C9B458;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;spacingRight=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10